# Linkzly Web SDK

Follow the [linkzly-web-sdk](../skills/linkzly-web-sdk/SKILL.md) skill for every step. It holds the order of work and a reference file for each section of the Linkzly Web SDK docs.

Three rules hold even if you read nothing else:

- Never make up an SDK key. Ask the person for it.
- Call `configure` once per page load, in the browser. It sends the install, open and session-end events itself, so do not call `trackFirstVisit` or `trackOpen`.
- Every custom event name has to be registered for the app in the Linkzly console, or the event is dropped while the call succeeds. `page_view`, `time_on_page`, `scroll_depth` and `outbound_click` are built in and need no registration.
